# Fact patterns — paid sick leave accrual

Generated from `corpus/gold/fact_patterns.jsonl` (FP-017 … FP-025). Each pattern names the
branch it is meant to take; the three statutory-floor branches are the compliance bug the
system exists to catch.

> Using Legal_types as T
> Using Sick_leave_accrual_acme as S

## FP-017 — handbook 1:40 (SYN-005 § 4.2.1); Washington's statute states the same ratio

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFp017:
  output computation content S.SickLeaveAccrual

scope TestFp017:
  definition computation equals
    output of S.SickLeaveAccrual with {
      -- hours_worked: 1200.0
      -- weeks_worked: 30
      -- work_state: T.WorkState.WA
      -- days_employed: 365
      -- exempt: false
    }
  assertion computation.accrual_divisor = 40.0
  assertion computation.accrued_hours = 30.0
  assertion computation.annual_use_cap = 40.0
  assertion computation.usable = true
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestFp017
┌─[RESULT]─ TestFp017 ─
│ computation =
│   SickLeaveAccrual {
│     -- accrual_divisor: 40.0
│     -- accrued_hours: 30.0
│     -- annual_use_cap: 40.0
│     -- usable: true
│   }
└─
```

